  "note": "Finding (ai), found by steering with seed 11 after the D25 amendment (a node's own bottom margin never moves it); reduced from document 40. A text keeps its lines on a page and loses the bottom margin that crosses the page end, so the view around it ends on that page with its bottom padding and margin below the page end. The rest of the outer view kept the box of the whole view, higher than what it still held by the room the page took plus that part (in the unreduced document 266.8 pt against a content area of 223 pt), so the cut of the next page held back the link after it, which starts above the page end, and the graft threw 'Pagination held back content that starts above the page end' (production laid the whole part out instead). Fixed: the split reports how far a node that ends on the page reaches below the page end (restOverhang, paginate/split-parts.ts), and the cut of the rest allows for it (layOutRest, paginate/index.ts). Rows: test/pagination-cut.test.ts, 'a node that ends at the page end with its bottom margin below it' and '... padding below it'.",
